From c8af0b7a8cb980cdea9cb32eefc3a206e2b1c483 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 18:29:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] perf(preview): share one copy of node_modules instead of
 one per project
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Keeping idle sandboxes rather than deleting them is what removes the reinstall
on reopen, but it raised a fair question: at ~300MB of node_modules each, does
that just trade a slow preview for a full disk?

Measured first. The scaffold's dependency tree is 301MB across 28,199 files,
plus a 118MB npm cache. Fifty idle projects would be 15GB — a real objection.

It does not have to be per-project. Image layers are shared read-only across
every container on a host, and a container's own storage holds only what it
CHANGES. So installing the dependencies at /home/node/app — the exact directory
the sandbox runs from — means every preview reads one shared copy, and each
container costs only its source plus whatever that project added on top. Fifty
idle projects become one 301MB layer and fifty small deltas.

The previous arrangement actively prevented that, and was worse than doing
nothing: it staged the modules at /opt/lm-base and hardlinked them in with
`cp -al` at boot. On overlayfs a hardlink out of a lower layer forces a
copy-up, so every container materialised the full 301MB into its own writable
layer anyway — paying the disk cost while looking like it was avoiding it. The
staging and the copy are both gone; npm now reconciles the image's tree in
place, leaving matching packages untouched in the shared layer and writing only
genuine differences.

For hosts still on plain node:22-alpine, where each container really does hold
its own copy, the GC gains a MAX_STOPPED cap (default 20): beyond that, the
least recently used stopped sandboxes are removed. Sorted by when each was last
stopped rather than by age, so a project someone opens daily outranks one
created yesterday and abandoned. Bounds disk at roughly N x 300MB regardless of
how many projects exist, and never binds at all on the prebuilt image.

tsc --noEmit: 47 before, 47 after. Build passes, 33 tests pass, and both the
installer and the generated GC script are checked with bash -n.
